# Plan

Full route: configuration ownership and many execution consumers change.
D-01 / R-01: Adopt Ec declarative catalog and native/rules layout, adapting its frontend, PostgreSQL and browser services as not applicable to Rust/Iced Ox. Preserve CLI scopes and existing security policy rather than copying Ec-specific exception decisions.
D-02 / R-02: Keep shell adapters and native report validation; validated data is never evaluated as shell code. Move policies, preserve their semantics and migrate callers.
D-03 / R-03: Preserve historical evidence; tests establish configuration contracts, not successful real scans or GUI acceptance.

Selected and consulted primary: software-delivery, .codex/skills/software-delivery/SKILL.md; bridge sdd/chain/software-delivery.md version 1. Contribution: input inventory, controlled execution and failure verification. Consulted references/build-inputs-and-trust.md. Actual source hashes are in the validation inventory. No delegation.

## Default parity successor

D-04 / R-04: Supersede D-01 only where it preserved the old CLI/default selection.
Adopt plan/run, complete without filters, default surfaces and mandatory docs;
map the desktop workspace to application. Preserve legacy flag-only calls for
existing consumers. Planning must not execute Cargo or scanners. Use validated
catalog projections; never evaluate data as shell. Shared environment defaults
exclude Ec service variables and automatic database maintenance.

Continue the consulted software-delivery skill and bridge version 1 identified
above; its build-input reference guides the parity inventory, controlled fixtures
and separation of configuration acceptance from a complete native run.

D-05 / R-05: Apply common Ruff/ShellCheck/Bandit/Syft/Grype/Trivy policies and
Clippy groups; adapt Rust/EICAR indicators and scanner deadlines. Retain Ox
licenses, reviewed dependency generations, advisory exceptions and static baseline.
Expanded Trivy results require counting all scanner findings and projecting secret
values/code out before persistence, with raw identity/loss metadata. Native fixture
probes establish policy loading/detection, not a clean full checkout or universal
scanner effectiveness. No external catalogs or new CodeQL execution engine are
claimed by this change.

## Complete-run remediation successor

D-06 / R-06: Preserve configured analyzer groups; fix source defects and apply only source-bound reviewed dispositions for intentional predicates/module interfaces. Validate real exit/error propagation rather than silencing failures. Do not infer coverage from partial Geiger output. Keep current Iced generation; review exact dependency edges and licenses before policy changes.

Continue primary software-delivery at .codex/skills/software-delivery/SKILL.md and sdd/chain/software-delivery.md version 1; consulted build-inputs-and-trust.md for tool/dataset provenance and verification. Supporting rust (.codex/skills/rust/SKILL.md; sdd/chain/rust.md version 1) addresses Rust 1.99/edition 2024 lints and preserved behavior; application-security (.codex/skills/application-security/SKILL.md; sdd/chain/application-security.md version 1) addresses reviewed datasets, dependency policy and detection fixtures. All three entries were actually read. No delegation.

## Cargo discovery and portable evidence successor

D-07 / R-07: Follow Ec's PATH-first discovery, appending
`OX_CARGO_BIN` or `${CARGO_HOME:-$HOME/.cargo}/bin`; reject an explicitly empty
override. This supersedes only the local-cache-first selection introduced by
T005. Give adapter fixtures a private CARGO_HOME and plugin directory. Keep the
installed Ox toolchain pin, locked/offline arguments, native binary identity and
strict per-member reports. Adopt Ec's configured 16 MiB Geiger thread stack and
all-features selection without changing host limits or scanner installations.

D-08 / R-08: Keep this feature in governance copies. Preserve the previous
composite evidence bytes under the successor validation record, then replace
current evidence with observations scoped to portable script/configuration
inputs. Earlier criteria affected by these changes remain INCONCLUSIVE until
independently reevaluated; do not regenerate hashes to reuse a prior result.
Invalidate only bound observations affected in dependency-hygiene, retaining its
prior bytes. Excluding this feature or copying Cargo caches into the package
would conceal the scope mismatch and is rejected.

